# Batch 1d nexus lane rename map (old new); see model/README.md "Sealing a batch".
#
# fn-159.5 bound renames (nexus use sites). A Query's receipt records its bound by bare name, and the
# step tables record no bounds, so these are not word renames here: `four four` cannot say "only in
# the close policy's receipts". For the IR comparison after Batch 5b's regeneration:
#   nexus workflow `control`              -> Bounds.eight      (same budget 8/8/262144)
#   close policy `four`/`five`/`twelve`   -> fourWide/fiveWide/twelveWide (budgets unchanged)
#   nexus workflow `two`                  -> Bounds.two        (name unchanged)
#
# fn-160 R13 and fn-160.6 (owner): the Nexus Product moves to shared/product, and the System level
# becomes Protocol (system/ -> protocol/, NexusSystem -> NexusProtocol).
temporal.features.nexus.product temporal.features.nexus.shared.product
temporal.features.nexus.standalone.system temporal.features.nexus.standalone.protocol
temporal.features.nexus.workflow.system temporal.features.nexus.workflow.protocol
nexusSystem nexusProtocol
